 "_about": "Chang'e-4 (CNSA): the first soft landing on the far side of the Moon, with the Yutu-2 rover; it talks to Earth through the Queqiao relay satellite, about 65,000 km beyond the Moon at the Earth-Moon L2 point. Launch 7 Dec 2018 18:23 UTC on a Long March 3B from Xichang; lunar orbit 12 Dec 08:45 UTC (100 km); perilune lowered to 15 km 30 Dec 00:55 UTC; landing 3 Jan 2019 02:26 UTC in Von Karman crater (Statio Tianhe). APPROXIMATE: powered descent start (~11 minutes before landing) and Yutu-2 rolling onto the surface (~22:22 Beijing time, about 12 hours after landing). The trajectory is ILLUSTRATED; not flight data.",
